  "tier": "told-once",
  "plain": "After the 1969 Apollo 11 Moon mission, the astronaut Michael Collins is said to have told a press conference that the crew could not see any stars, while his own later book describes it differently. Michels tells this himself, comparing the press conference with Collins's book, which he does not name. He raises it because, if the two accounts clash, it would raise questions about what the astronauts were saying in public."
